# Final products
/wiimc.elf
/wiimc.dol

# Filled by `make -f Makefile.gc` when the SD card is plugged in: every ELF
# that went onto the card, and every log that came back from it
/deployed/
/logs/
*.elf.map

# The build/ directory is not ignored wholesale: build/wiimc.ld and
# build/wiimc.spec are part of the tree and must stay tracked. Only what the
# compiler puts there is ignored.
/build/*.o
/build/*.d
/build/*.h
/build/*.ii
/build/*.lst
/build/*.map
/build/*.s

# MPlayer and FFmpeg are built in place, inside source/mplayer, so their
# leavings have to be ignored where they fall.
#
# Upstream had committed 319 .d files and the 5 .o files under
# source/mplayer/ffmpeg/libavcodec/libopus/. Ignoring a pattern does not
# untrack what is already committed, so every build rewrote them and left ~160
# files showing as modified -- enough noise to hide a real change in
# `git status`. They are untracked now (`git rm --cached`, the files stay on
# disk). Nothing needs them: all five .o have their .c beside them, and every
# .d is regenerated by -MD -MP on the next compile.
#
# If a merge from upstream ever brings them back, remove them again rather
# than committing the churn.
*.o
*.a
*.d
*.ho
source/mplayer/ffmpeg/libavutil/avconfig.h

# Host tools the cross build makes for itself
source/mplayer/codec-cfg
source/mplayer/codec-cfg.exe
source/mplayer/ffmpeg/**/*_tablegen
source/mplayer/ffmpeg/**/*_tablegen.exe

# Editor and OS droppings
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
